<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A1.T4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantitative Results for Kaleido Design Ablations.</span> We report the complete quantitative results (PSNR, higher is better) corresponding to the ablation study in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ (ii) Unified Positional Encoding for Space and Time ‣ 3.2.1 Designing Kaledio’s Design Spaces ‣ 3.2 Kaleido Architecture Details and Training Strategies ‣ 3 Kaleido: Scaling Rectified Flow Transformers for Generative Rendering ‣ Scaling Sequence-to-Sequence GenerativeNeural Rendering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Performance is evaluated in one-to-five, five-to-one, and five-to-five reference-to-target view settings. Our final design choice for each component is marked in red. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Details of Kaleido Training Strategies</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All Kaleido model variants are trained using the same datasets detailed in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Training Configurations and Evaluation Strategy ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Scaling Sequence-to-Sequence GenerativeNeural Rendering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, with the AdamW optimiser <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov and Hutter, 2019</a>)</cite> and a weight decay of <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. In each training iteration, we randomly sample a total of 12 frames per sequence. These frames are then partitioned into reference and target views according to the view sampling strategy in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS1" title="3.2.1 Designing Kaledio’s Design Spaces ‣ 3.2 Kaleido Architecture Details and Training Strategies ‣ 3 Kaleido: Scaling Rectified Flow Transformers for Generative Rendering ‣ Scaling Sequence-to-Sequence GenerativeNeural Rendering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The learning rate is chosen based on the training stage. For the initial video pre-training and the first stage of 3D fine-tuning (both at 256px resolution), we apply a learning rate of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the subsequent high-resolution 3D fine-tuning stages (512px and 1024px resolution), we decrease the learning rate to <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>. To train our larger models at high resolutions, we incorporate FSDP sharding and activation checkpointing.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Across all stages, we use <span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fp16</span> mixed-precision training, as we find it crucial for stable training convergence; while <span id="A2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bf16</span> consistently leads to unstable training. Our largest Kaleido model is trained for two weeks on 512 NVIDIA H100 GPUs. Additional hyper-parameters are listed in Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Additional Details of Kaleido Training Strategies ‣ Scaling Sequence-to-Sequence GenerativeNeural Rendering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
